eq 0 ). Hence, having the neural network predict 𝒙 𝟎  m{x_{0}} directly is preferred for broader applicability and improved generalizability. Notably, the mean is continuous at γ = 0 \gamma=0 (see Appendix A.2 ), thus there are no problems during gradient computation, such as taking gradients where a function is not differentiable. Nonetheless, for each specific value of γ \gamma , the mean is continuous and the γ \gamma constant hyperparameter is immutable, i.e., set only once for each model instance, thereby no discontinuity issues would ever arise due to γ \gamma .

